+// Reader/Web page back. Closing on PRESSED (touch-DOWN) was the fix for the V4
+// cap-touch swipe detector: it calls lv_indev_wait_release mid-tap and drops the
+// bar's CLICKED, so the reader's "‹" tap "did nothing". But touch-down is also a
+// trap while reading: a finger that lands on the bar and then drags — the first
+// few pixels of a scroll that starts a touch too high — left the page before the
+// drag had moved at all, so scrolling a long page could quit the reader. Wait for
+// the release instead and only take it as a tap: movement beyond kSbTapSlop px,
+// or a press long enough to be the screenshot hold, is not back. RELEASED is as
+// reliable as PRESSED (wait_release skips CLICKED, not RELEASED), so the
+// cap-touch trap stays closed.
+static constexpr lv_coord_t kSbTapSlop = 12;   // px of finger travel that make it a drag
+static lv_coord_t s_sb_tap_x = 0, s_sb_tap_y = 0;
+static uint32_t   s_sb_tap_start_ms = 0;
